    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_AboutCapabilities">Session Controller Manager identifies which controllers are connected and active, combining data from the Playnite SDK, XInput and SDL to build a reliable picture of who is playing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_AboutCapabilities2">When a controller disconnects during a game session, the plugin shows a full-screen external overlay with the controller name and pause status. It can suspend the game process automatically — compatible with any game, no key configuration needed — and resumes as soon as a controller reconnects or another one takes over.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_AboutCapabilities3">Includes customizable notifications for both Desktop and Fullscreen modes: colors, font sizes, position, padding, border and icon layout are all configurable separately for each mode. The top-bar icon shows the primary controller and uses color to indicate battery level.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_AboutCapabilities4">Battery reporting works with DualSense, DualShock 4, Xbox controllers and any SDL-supported device. Connection type (USB, Bluetooth, wireless) is detected automatically.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_AboutSafety">Its external overlay and optional pause actions are isolated from Playnite and the game. It avoids input injection and falls back conservatively whenever device, process or online-session evidence is incomplete.</sys:String>
